- {"summary": "The paper identifies DPO's misspecification problem in non-tabular policy classes, analyzes its failure modes geometrically, and proposes AuxDPO with auxiliary variables to mitigate these issues, showing empirical improvements.", "significance_and_novelty": "Identifies and fixes a fundamental misspecification problem in DPO through geometric analysis and auxiliary variables, with empirical gains in LLM alignment.", "reasons_for_acceptance": ["The paper identifies a significant theoretical limitation of DPO (misspecification in non-tabular policy classes) and provides a rigorous geometric analysis (Section 3).", "The proposed AuxDPO method offers a principled solution to DPO's misspecification problem by introducing auxiliary variables (Section 4.2).", "Empirical results demonstrate AuxDPO's superior performance over DPO and other baselines on real-world LLM alignment tasks (Section 5).", "The local geometry analysis of both DPO and RLHF provides novel insights into their relationship (Section 4.1)."], "reasons_for_rejection": ["The theoretical analysis is limited to the large-\u03b2 regime (local approximation), which may not fully capture practical DPO implementations (Section 4.1).", "The empirical evaluation could benefit from more diverse baseline comparisons (e.g., PPO-based RLHF) to better establish AuxDPO's advantages (Section 5).", "The paper does not provide a comprehensive analysis of computational overhead introduced by AuxDPO's auxiliary variables (Section 4.2)."], "suggestions": ["Include a more detailed complexity analysis of AuxDPO compared to standard DPO (Section 4.2).", "Expand the empirical evaluation to include PPO-based RLHF as an additional baseline (Section 5).", "Discuss practical guidelines for setting the \u03bb hyperparameter in AuxDPO (Section 4.2).", "Provide more intuition about the geometric interpretation of the auxiliary variables (Figure 3)."], "rating": 7, "confidence": 4, "soundness": 3, "presentation": 3, "contribution": 3}

- {"summary": "The paper analyzes DPO's misspecification when reward functions are unrealizable, proposes AuxDPO with auxiliary variables to better approximate RLHF, and shows empirical gains on preference alignment tasks.", "significance_and_novelty": "Identifies DPO's misspecification problem via geometric analysis and proposes AuxDPO with auxiliary reward-space variables to mitigate it.", "reasons_for_acceptance": ["The paper identifies a significant limitation in DPO (misspecification) and proposes a principled solution (AuxDPO) with theoretical grounding (Section 3).", "AuxDPO demonstrates consistent empirical improvements over DPO across multiple benchmark datasets (REWARDBENCH V2 and MMLU-PRO) and settings (Section 5).", "The geometric characterization of DPO's limitations provides novel insights into preference optimization (Section 1)."], "reasons_for_rejection": ["The theoretical guarantees of AuxDPO are only valid locally (at high \u03b2 values), limiting their general applicability (Section 5).", "The paper lacks ablation studies to isolate the impact of auxiliary variables from other algorithmic components (Section 4.2).", "Experimental comparisons with other state-of-the-art methods (e.g., PPO-based RLHF) are insufficient to claim broad superiority (Section 5)."], "suggestions": ["Include a sensitivity analysis of \u03b2 to demonstrate the practical range where local guarantees hold.", "Add comparisons with full two-stage RLHF (PPO) to contextualize AuxDPO's performance gap.", "Clarify the computational overhead of auxiliary variables in large-scale LLM training."], "rating": 7, "confidence": 4, "soundness": 3, "presentation": 3, "contribution": 3}

